CCC CSNT1200F26 Intro to Networking Fall 2026

IP addresses are categorized in classes, A B C identified by the first byte of the number
Class A has values 1-127   - default subnet is 255.0.0.0
Class B has values 128-191 - default subnet is 255.255.0.0
Class C has values 192-223 - default subnet is 255.255.255.0

Subnet is the part of an address that is the same for all things on the network - think like 'Main St' of '123 Main St Corning NY'

By changing the variable part of a subnet mask you can create custom subnets which are smaller networks within the larger one, allowing for 123 Main St Apt 1 and 123 Main St Apt 2

DNS is the phone book of the internet



Ethernet cables are 'twisted pair'

ASK FOR HELP!!

To get an A read ahead.

Pay attention to the details.

Routers start shutdown, Switches auto start.

Router>   User EXEC - limited commands
Router#   Priviledged EXEC - all the commands

Physical address is the mac address
ipv4 addresses are private, only used locally

Multilayer switches provide limited router functionality with switch functionality

Different subnet masks indicate different networks, require communication through the router.

Switches don't use an actual ip address, interact through the virtual terminal vlan1
